---
// ── Comparison ────────────────────────────────────────
---

<section class="section">
  <div class="section-title">How it compares</div>
  <div class="tbl-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th></th>
          <th>Containers</th>
          <th>Traditional VMs</th>
          <th class="pichi">pichi</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <th>Isolation</th>
          <td>Shared host kernel</td>
          <td>Full VM boundary</td>
          <td class="pichi">Full VM boundary</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th>Portability</th>
          <td>One image, many hosts</td>
          <td>Tied to hypervisor &amp; format</td>
          <td class="pichi">One image, laptop → cloud → bare metal</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th>Boot trusted base</th>
          <td>Host's — inherited</td>
          <td>Large UEFI firmware</td>
          <td class="pichi">Tiny boot stub, no large UEFI firmware</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th>Attestation</th>
          <td>None at boot</td>
          <td>Hard — firmware varies</td>
          <td class="pichi">Deterministic launch measurement; hardware attestation on the roadmap*</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th>Workflow</th>
          <td>pull / push / run</td>
          <td>Bespoke tooling</td>
          <td class="pichi">pull / push / run over OCI</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p class="caveat">
    These are real virtual machines — heavier than a container, far lighter than a traditional VM.
    <br />*Hardware attestation targets confidential-computing platforms (AMD SEV-SNP, with Intel
    TDX and Arm CCA drafted) and is planned, not yet shipping.
  </p>
</section>

<style>
  .tbl-wrap {
    overflow-x: auto;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 10px;
  }
  table {
    border-collapse: collapse;
    width: 100%;
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    min-width: 34rem;
  }
  th,
  td {
    text-align: left;
    padding: 0.85rem 1rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    vertical-align: top;
  }
  thead th {
    background: var(--surface);
    color: #fff;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  thead th.pichi {
    color: var(--green);
  }
  tbody th {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--fg);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  td.pichi {
    color: #fff;
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(63, 185, 80, 0.05), transparent);
  }
  tbody tr:last-child th,
  tbody tr:last-child td {
    border-bottom: none;
  }
  .caveat {
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-top: 0.9rem;
    text-align: center;
  }
</style>
